commit 6a86021519b2da6d8bf8914d2027e24b040c87d9

C03: bluetooth.radio.status reads whether the Bluetooth radio is on; constraint ack publishes its kept sentence (NETWORK1457)

NETWORK1301 documented that «tengo el bluetooth encendido» (H0445) and «y el bluetooth?» (H0466) had no radio-state read in the catalog: bluetooth.device.list enumerates devices and bluetooth.radio.set only observes the state as the post-read of a change. WEB1455 measured that the constraint acknowledgement's first-sentence clip validated the shortened text but published message.content unchanged.

Baxy.Kernel ProductCatalog: descriptor bluetooth.radio.status (no arguments, ReadOnly, verifier bluetooth.radio.status.windows.radio.read.v1), in ordinal order after bluetooth.radio.set.
Baxy.Core ExternalCapabilityHandlers: the operation is handled.
Baxy.Providers.Windows WindowsDeviceControlAdapter: BluetoothRadioStatusAsync reads the Bluetooth radios through the official Windows Radio API and reports seen.radioOn, radioCount and radiosOn without changing anything; WindowsExternalCapabilityProvider maps its unavailability reason like the other Bluetooth operations.
baxy_mind effect_intent: _bluetooth_state_question reads «tengo/tenés el bluetooth encendido|prendido|apagado|activado», «el bluetooth está …», «está encendido el bluetooth» and the antecedent-less «y el bluetooth?» as a bluetooth.radio.status read (never a device list; not with headphones or devices named), accepted as a direct request and grounded by the domain noun.
baxy_mind __main__: the read takes no arguments.
baxy_mind llm: an instruction says seen.radioOn true is on and false is off; the reply must carry the observed state (missing_state), must not invert it (reversed_state, negations such as «no está encendido» or «no tienes el bluetooth encendido» read as the off state) and must not claim a change (extra_claim); the constraint acknowledgement now publishes the sentence it kept.
Catalog aliases: one row for the read (alias_count 159); documentación/base/05_MATRIZ_EJECUCION.json: the read is registered as read-only without effect.

Offline probes: the two literals and both variants resolve to one bluetooth.radio.status; the boundaries resolve to nothing and «No apagues el bluetooth.» is a prohibition; over an observed radioOn=false, «El bluetooth está encendido» and «Sí, tienes el bluetooth encendido» are vetoed while «No, el bluetooth está apagado» and «El bluetooth no está encendido» pass. Providers project compiled clean before sealing (build servers shut down). Kernel, Core, Providers and App recompiled (BUILD1457). Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


